  'Sputtering spittle and loudly passing value judgments on others is low-grade. —— Wang Xiaobo',
  'When speaking of others, first treat him as an ordinary person, then discuss his good and evil, right and wrong. —— Wang Xiaobo',
  'Loyalty to known facts is called honesty; disloyalty to facts is called hypocrisy. There are also those loyal only to selected facts — this is neither honesty nor hypocrisy; I call it bluster. —— Wang Xiaobo',
  'Ruffianism is bad, but its root is not moral; the real cause is impoverishment. —— Wang Xiaobo',
  'Goodness must be built on truth; so if I must choose a moral foundation, I would choose seeking truth from facts. —— Wang Xiaobo',
  'Better to be taken for a fool with your mouth shut than to open it and dispel every doubt. —— Wang Xiaobo',
  'A person must have a theme in life, something that haunts his dreams. —— Wang Xiaobo',
  "The years flow on, like the moon hanging in the sky, shining on each of us — yet everyone's life is different. —— Wang Xiaobo",
  'In this world, you need not know everything; it is enough to know only the best. —— Wang Xiaobo',
  'It is easy for a person to be romantic about things he does not understand. —— Wang Xiaobo',
  'Life is a lonely road; it needs an interesting book to while away the journey. —— Wang Xiaobo',
